    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαρμακός</span></b>  [v. ad fin.], ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one sacrificed</i>
			or <i>executed as an atonement</i> or <i>purification</i> for
			others, <i>scapegoat,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
				5
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				733
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				Ister
				33
			</span></i>; and, since criminals were reserved for this fate, a general
			name of reproach, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1405
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.53
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διηγήσεις</span></u>
				 ii 29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				25.80
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
			</span></i> l.c.; on the accent v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
			</span></i> Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.150
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαρμᾶκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Did.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>]</div>
